      "justification": "Lines 8 and 10 compute t1 = x1 * w1 and t2 = x2 * w2 in double. 0.8 has no exact binary64 form, so 0.8 * 1.5 is the double 1.2000000000000002. %+g (7.21.6.1p8, conversion g): the precision is omitted, so P = 6; in style e the value would have exponent X = 0, and P > X >= -4, so it is converted in style f with precision P - (X + 1) = 5, giving 1.20000; the g conversion then removes the trailing zeros, giving 1.2, and the + flag (7.21.6.1p6) adds the sign: +1.2. 0.4 * -1 is exactly the negated double of 0.4; with X = -1 the same rule gives -0.400000, trimmed to -0.4. Captured run lines 1-2.",
